It's not so much a hack for windows, but it has to do with the fact
that there are about 3 or 4 different ways to write to the console in
Windows, and capturing the output from any of varies from simple pipes
to more complex hooks and memory tricks. Nethack doesn't use any
special "trick" to output in Windows so much as Windows uses several
different "standards" that don't all have easy access for peeking at
other processes.



